{% comment %}
  The home page body: a list of pieces, the newest first. Kept out of
  _pages/home.md so it stays indented — prettier flattens HTML nested in the
  Markdown page. Wrapped in one element so kramdown passes it through untouched.
  Each piece is something to play with, then a line on where it leads.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="home">
  <p class="pieces-intro">Mertcan Özdemir · MRI, ice hockey, small electronics</p>

  <div class="pieces">
    <section class="piece is-lead" aria-labelledby="piece-kspace" data-kspace>
      <div class="piece-art kspace">
        <figure>
          <canvas data-k role="img" aria-label="k-space, filled line by line as the scan goes"></canvas>
          <figcaption>k-space</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <canvas data-img role="img" aria-label="The cat, rebuilt from the lines measured"></canvas>
          <figcaption data-caption>the cat</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="kspace-controls">
          <p class="kspace-plans" role="group" aria-label="Scan">
            <button type="button" data-plan="linear">every line, top to bottom <span data-time></span></button>
            <button type="button" data-plan="centric">every line, centre first <span data-time></span></button>
            <button type="button" data-plan="fourth">every fourth line <span data-time></span></button>
            <button type="button" data-plan="centre">only the centre <span data-time></span></button>
          </p>
          <p class="kspace-status">
            <span data-clock></span>
            <span data-status aria-live="polite"></span>
            <button type="button" data-unfold aria-pressed="false" hidden>unfold with 8 coils</button>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="piece-text">
        <h2 class="piece-title" id="piece-kspace">Why does an MRI take so long?</h2>
        <p class="piece-desc">
          A scanner does not take a picture: it measures k‑space, the image's frequencies, one line at a time, and each line takes half a second (here
          they go eight times as fast). Today's patient is a cat, and it keeps still for about half a minute. Scan every line and it takes over a
          minute; scan fewer and see what it costs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <a class="piece is-lead is-flip" href="{{ '/play/' | relative_url }}">
      <span class="piece-art piece-drill" data-game="still">
        <svg viewBox="-30.6 -16.8 61.2 34.2" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
      </span>
      <span class="piece-text">
        <span class="piece-title">Three on three</span>
        <span class="piece-desc">A small hockey game against the computer, which has been practising.</span>
        <span class="piece-more">Play&nbsp;→</span>
      </span>
    </a>

    <a class="piece is-lead" href="{{ '/drills/' | relative_url }}">
      <span class="piece-art piece-drill" data-drill="two-on-one-give-and-go" data-preview>
        <svg viewBox="-30.6 -16.8 61.2 34.2" aria-hidden="true">
          <g class="trails"></g>
          <g class="events"></g>
          <g class="actors"></g>
        </svg>
      </span>
      <span class="piece-text">
        <span class="piece-title">Hockey drills, animated</span>
        <span class="piece-desc">Fifty-two practice drills, skated by small round players who never get tired.</span>
        <span class="piece-more">See the drills&nbsp;→</span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>
</div>
